{"type":"thinking","text":"Let me understand the puzzle deeply. This seems to be a scenario with a subtle trap: the original receipt from run DUTY-2340 at 23:40 claims certain limits/actual, but the current desk says shift-plan.json is current班表, and \"DESK-21 为 21:00 同班冷夜数字站控台架的交流电表采集，线上参数按适用记录的采集时间生效。本地 node operations/retest.mjs 按这份记录复算。\"\n\nThe release-format.md says:\n- archived original receipt for this shift's vehicle test rig is in operations/original-receipt.json; conditions and applicability see within.\n- depot directory registers previous duty maintainers; depot_trial's range for this seat is the original 21:00 public capture.\n- Scheduling keeps current fields, two-vehicle windows, 20 kW reserved shift, and maximum available charging energy under high-efficiency condition.\n- Per-vehicle decisions based on vehicle's available net energy at departure.\n- Revise shift-plan.json, HANDOVER.md, create release.json.\n- release.json fields: departureKwh & marginKwh each arrays of values for 90% in A/B order; at90, at85 each {\"A\":\"GO or HOLD\",\"B\":\"GO or HOLD\"}; evidenceSha is the full Git SHA pointed to by the basis record. Negative margin means gap.\n- Handover notes basis, final two-vehicle departure amounts, margins, per-vehicle/low efficiency disposition. Original materials preserved as-is. If saving a new rig receipt, put it in operations/revision-receipt.json.\n\nNow there's a subtlety: The original-receipt.json claims \"limits\": [80,40,50,70] but \"actual\": [80,40,50,50], and departureKwh [126,121], withinLimits false. It has sha 341e19e... which is the \"Open morning release with desk meter reading at 21:00\" commit. The claimed limits [80,40,50,70] are different from what cold-cycle.json and retest.mjs calculate. Let's compute retest limits from cold-cycle: each sample 30 min, (end-start)*60/30 = (end-start)*2. Slot 0: (6040-6000)*2 = 80. Slot 1: (6060-6040)*2 = 40. Slot 2: (6095-6060)*2 = 70. Slot 3: (6120-6095)*2 = 50. So limits = [80,40,70,50]. Actual = min(limits, plan.acKw) = [80,40,70,50] since plan is [80,40,70,50]. departureKwh = [72+0.45*(80+40), 76+0.45*(70+50)] = [72+54,76+54] = [126,130]. withinLimits true.\n\nBut original-receipt.json says limits [80,40,50,70] and actual [80,40,50,50], departure [126,121], withinLimits false. That contradicts the current 21:00 capture. Hmm. The original receipt is archived from 23:40 DUTY-2340, and its applicability says \"站型 R4。站控交流上限按时段固定；四格半小时、两车窗口、20 kW 平移不变时，可将该上限用于窗口内的新设定。\" (station type R4. Station-controlled AC limits fixed by time slot; when four half-hour slots, two-vehicle windows, 20kW shift unchanged, this limit may be used for new settings within the window.)\n\nSo there's a conflict between the original receipt's limits [80,40,50,70] and the 21:00 cold-cycle capture [80,40,70,50]. Which one should govern? The desk says \"DESK-21 为 21:00 同班冷夜数字站控台架的交流电表采集，线上参数按适用记录的采集时间生效。本地 node operations/retest.mjs 按这份记录复算。\" Translation: DESK-21 is the AC meter capture from the 21:00 same-shift cold-night digital station control rig; online parameters take effect according to the capture time of the applicable record. Local retest.mjs recomputes according to this record.\n\nrelease-format says \"归档的本班原表车辆台架回执见 operations/original-receipt.json，工况与适用范围见单内。调度台名录登记值班维护者，depot_trial 的本席量程为原 21:00 公开采集。\" The archived original sheet vehicle rig receipt is original-receipt.json, conditions and applicability in the sheet. The depot directory registers duty maintainers; depot_trial's range for this seat is the original 21:00 public capture.\n\n\"depot_trial 的本席量程为原 21:00 公开采集\" - depot_trial's measurement range for this seat is the original 21:00 public capture. So the official measurement basis is cold-cycle.json (21:00), not the 23:40 receipt? Let me think.\n\nThe original-receipt has captureDigest 4a372... maybe digest of cold-cycle.json? Let's check. Also sheetBlob 909e4... maybe blob of shift-plan? Let me compute git hashes. Actually git blob hashes for file