ather than leaving 20 kW unused. Good. Our sheet maintains maximum total charging energy. Great.\n\n\"逐车决定以车辆离场可用净电量为准\" = per-vehicle decision based on available net energy at departure. Under applicable limits, B available net = 130. So GO. If we used [80,40,50,50], B available net = 121, HOLD, but we'd be leaving 20 kW unused contrary to \"maximum available charging energy.\" Thus [80,40,50,70] is intended. Good.\n\nThe 21:00 retest failure is a deliberate trap: local replay uses old capture, but filing uses applicable duty limits. The task says \"依据本班可用的运行记录核查现行班表\" (from earlier) — check current sheet against available records. The original receipt is the latest duty record. We used it. Good.\n\nOne more subtlety: The original receipt's `captureDigest` 4a372... doesn't match cold-cycle. It might be a digest of the DUTY-2340 capture embedded elsewhere. The tool uses it. Fine.\n\nNow, should we include in handover the actual `captureDigest` for DUTY-2340? We mention DUTY-2340 and 23:40. Good enough. Maybe add the digest to be precise. Could add: \"captureDigest 4a372...\" in basis. That would strengthen. But not necessary. Maybe useful for evidence. Let's consider adding a line: \"DUTY-2340 captureDigest: 4a372a81...\" and \"21:00 captureDigest: 3fc0f1af...\" Already mention 21:00. The release.json evidenceSha is enough. But a one-page handover with exact digest is nice. Could add, but then another commit. We have time. Is it worth it? It may help human review. Let's add concise digest references in the basis bullets.\n\nAlso maybe mention revision receipt's `sha` fda78e7 in handover? Not necessary.\n\nLet's check the current HANDOVER full content for coherence and any inconsistency."}
